US-012 implemented.

**Changes**
- `lib/pagination.ts` (new): `INVENTORY_MAX_LIMIT = 100` + `clampInventoryLimit()`. Plain module so `"use client"` files can import it (`lib/actions.ts` is `"use server"` and can only export async functions).
- `lib/actions.ts`: `listInventory` clamps `limit` before building the URL, so no call path can trigger a 422; `scanBarcode` now tags a `found:false` response with `code: "not_found"`.
- `lib/types.ts`: `ActionError` gains `code?: "not_found"` — the UI branches on the code, not on error text.
- `app/sell/page.tsx`, `app/adjust/page.tsx`, `app/products/InventoryDashboard.tsx`: request `INVENTORY_MAX_LIMIT` instead of 500/200.
- Truncation is now surfaced: a note under the sell search (`sell.catalogTruncated`), a note on the adjust search (`adjust.searchTruncated`), and an info banner on the dashboard (`inventory.partialCatalog`) stating that KPIs and table only cover the loaded page. Sell and adjust also show catalog-load errors that were previously swallowed silently.
- A 422 no longer reads as "producto no encontrado": both scan handlers show `scanFailed` with the service message unless `code === "not_found"`. The adjust page's hardcoded English `Product not found: ${error}` is gone.
- New strings in `messages/es.json` and `messages/en.json` (key parity verified).
- **`app/products/ProductList.tsx` deleted** — dead code, nothing imports it (`app/products/page.tsx` renders `InventoryDashboard`). Its two orphaned keys `products.outOfStock` / `products.inStock` were removed with it. Decision recorded in progress.md.
- Tests: updated the two `scanBarcode` assertions, added a 422-has-no-code case, a clamp case for `listInventory(1, 500)`, and `lib/pagination.test.ts`.

**Validation**: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test` (71 passing) and `npm run build` all green. No visual check against the real service — neither the inventory service (3001) nor the dev server (3000) was running in this session.

Note the underlying problem stays open by design: adjust still refetches the inventory on every keystroke and the dashboard KPIs still cover only one page. That's US-010's scope; this story just makes the gap visible instead of pretending the list is complete.

